## Code Modernization & Refactoring Suite

We have a structured modernization framework installed in `.agents/skills/code-modernization/`. When conducting audits, large refactorings, or migrations, Cursor's AI should proactively utilize these subagents and follow their respective workflows:

### Specialized Subagents

| Subagent | Role / Purpose | Instructions Path |
|-------|----------------|-------------------|
| `architecture-critic` | Reviews proposed architectures and refactored code against modern best practices. Acts as a skeptical reviewer to avoid over-engineering. | `.agents/skills/code-modernization/agents/architecture-critic.md` |
| `business-rules-extractor` | Mines domain logic, calculations, validations, and policies from legacy code into clean, testable specifications. | `.agents/skills/code-modernization/agents/business-rules-extractor.md` |
| `legacy-analyst` | Deep-reads historical code structures to build complete behavioral and dependency maps. | `.agents/skills/code-modernization/agents/legacy-analyst.md` |
| `security-auditor` | Adversarial security reviewer (OWASP Top 10, CWE, logic flaws, dependency CVEs, secret detection). | `.agents/skills/code-modernization/agents/security-auditor.md` |
| `test-engineer` | Writes characterization, contract, and equivalence tests to pin down existing behavior before transformation. | `.agents/skills/code-modernization/agents/test-engineer.md` |

### Modernization Commands / Workflows

- **`modernize-assess`**: Discovery & portfolio complexity analysis of technical debt.
- **`modernize-map`**: Topology mapping of call graphs and batch data flows.
- **`modernize-extract-rules`**: Isolating business logic from low-level code.
- **`modernize-brief`**: Generating a phased refactoring and transformation plan.
- **`modernize-reimagine`**: Architectural design of the clean modern equivalent.
- **`modernize-transform`**: Execution of idiomatic refactoring/rewrite.
- **`modernize-harden`**: Security vulnerability scanning and mitigation patch.

---

## Animation Guidelines (GSAP)
- Always use `useGSAP()` (never `useEffect`) for GSAP animations.
- Register plugins in `lib/gsap.ts` (`ScrollTrigger`, `SplitText`, `DrawSVG`, `Flip`).
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` using `gsap.matchMedia()`.
